1
00:00:00,939 --> 00:00:03,189
(Howard:)You fly to Moscow,
they take you to Kazakhstan.

2
00:00:03,358 --> 00:00:07,198
Then you get in a Russian Soyuz rocket
which shoots you into a low earth orbit.

3
00:00:07,362 --> 00:00:10,652
Or it just sits on the launch pad because
the Kazakhi mafia sold the rocket fuel...

4
00:00:10,824 --> 00:00:13,364
...on the black market, heh.

5
00:00:14,494 --> 00:00:16,534
(Bernadette:)Are those Russian rockets safe?

6
00:00:16,704 --> 00:00:17,784
(Howard:)Safe as it can be...

7
00:00:17,956 --> 00:00:20,916
...when it was buiIt by the folks
who brought you ChernobyI. Ha, ha.

8
00:00:23,169 --> 00:00:25,419
(Leonard:)I'd like to propose a toast.

9
00:00:25,588 --> 00:00:28,088
(Leonard:)The dream to go up into space
is one we all share...

10
00:00:28,258 --> 00:00:31,848
(Leonard:)...and Howard's making that a reality.
We're all very proud of you.

11
00:00:32,011 --> 00:00:33,091
(All:)Cheers.

12
00:00:34,848 --> 00:00:37,348
- That was a lovely toast. Kudos.
- Thank you.

13
00:00:37,517 --> 00:00:41,057
SimuItaneously, a festival
of cloying clichés. You sicken me.

14
00:00:49,529 --> 00:00:52,069
(Howard:)You're really quiet. Is everything okay?

15
00:00:53,241 --> 00:00:55,071
(Leonard:)Fine.

16
00:00:57,620 --> 00:00:58,950
(Bernadette:)Just a little tired.

17
00:00:59,122 --> 00:01:04,022
(Howard:)I hope not too tired because I'm feeling
particularly masculine right now.

